feat(web): the console opens on YOUR agent, not the network's

Connecting a wallet produced no surface of your own: the registry, the stats and
the treasury card all described the network, and the only wallet-aware panels
sat at the very bottom. So a connected user still had to hunt for themselves.

Adds a My Agent passport directly under the header - identity, earned score,
clearance - plus the fields the contracts already stored but nothing rendered:
bond, status, agent URI, distinct clients and settled volume (a new passport
route reads them live).

Also: the wallet's own agent is tagged "yours" in the registry and auto-selected
in the detail pane, and a passport is shareable via an agent query param.